{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1181","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1181","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1181\",\"parent_revision\":\"5688f49528310e483dabedb5c5abf9b13ca84d91df7323df8c1df778789633d7\",\"root_revision\":\"5688f49528310e483dabedb5c5abf9b13ca84d91df7323df8c1df778789633d7\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCurrent task files use markdown with YAML frontmatter. Consider converting to pure YAML to leverage multi-document YAML notation (--- separators). Additionally, enforce that task data files are only written via scripts (backlog.py, implementation_manager.py, split_task_file.py, task_status_hook.py) \u2014 never manually edited by agents. The swarm-task-planner agent generated tasks with YAML inside fenced code blocks which the parser couldn't read, causing null agents and NOT_STARTED defaults. This suggests the generation pipeline needs format validation.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nClaims checked: 3 | VERIFIED: 3 | REFUTED: 0 | INCONCLUSIVE: 0\\n\\n1. VERIFIED: Task files use markdown with YAML frontmatter (both YAML frontmatter and legacy markdown formats coexist; task_format.py has_yaml_frontmatter() checks for --- delimiters)\\n2. VERIFIED: swarm-task-planner template shows ```yaml fenced blocks wrapping --- frontmatter; has_yaml_frontmatter() requires content.startswith(\\\"---\\\\n\\\") so fenced blocks fail detection\\n3. VERIFIED: _create_empty_task_data() sets agent=None, status=TaskStatus.NOT_STARTED when parser can't read format; parse_task_from_frontmatter never reached\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nGoal: Prevent swarm-task-planner from generating unparseable task files by adding format validation to the generation pipeline.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Parser code location and behavior | AVAILABLE | task_format.py, implementation_manager.py\\n2. swarm-task-planner agent template | AVAILABLE | Both python3-development and development-harness copies\\n3. split_task_file.py writer | AVAILABLE | plugins/python3-development/scripts/split_task_file.py\\n4. TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md spec | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md\\n5. Actual failing task files as examples | DERIVABLE | git history may have examples\\n6. Pure YAML multi-document format evaluation | DERIVABLE | requires design analysis of tradeoffs\\n7. Script-only writes enforcement mechanism | DERIVABLE | needs architecture decision\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\nMissing: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer**, I want **Current task files use markdown with YAML frontmatter** so that **backlog items are tracked in GitHub**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Not specified\\n- **Priority**: \\n- **Added**: \\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-02)\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\nThe fenced code block issue is reproduced by examining the swarm-task-planner template at:\\n- plugins/python3-development/agents/swarm-task-planner.md lines 249-265\\n- plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md lines 248-264\\n\\nBoth templates show the task frontmatter wrapped in a fenced yaml code block. The parser at task_format.py line 78 requires content.startswith(\\\"---\\n\\\") \u2014 a fenced block fails this check and falls through to legacy markdown parsing, which finds no ## Task header, returning an empty list.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 The fenced-code-block bug in swarm-task-planner causes null agents and NOT_STARTED defaults on every generated plan, requiring manual correction. Script-only writes enforcement prevents a parallel class of silent corruption. Both are correctness issues in the task file pipeline.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Any SAM plan generated by swarm-task-planner where the planner uses the documented template \u2014 tasks produce agent: null, status: not-started silently when the parser cannot read the fenced YAML block\\n- Bottleneck: /implement-feature queries ready-tasks from implementation_manager.py; null agents cause incorrect delegation or no delegation\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\nTwo targeted changes, scoped separately:\\n\\n1. Agent template fix: Remove the fenced yaml wrapper from the task structure template in both swarm-task-planner agent files so the model generates raw frontmatter\\n2. Format validator: Add a validation function (or extend parse_task_content) that raises an actionable error when has_yaml_frontmatter() returns False and the file appears to contain a fenced YAML block \u2014 instead of silently falling through to legacy parsing\\n3. Script-only writes policy: Document in TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md that task data files are written only by the four designated scripts; add a check in parse_task_content that warns when called on content that looks like manually written markdown bold-fields format\\n\\nNote: Pure YAML multi-document notation evaluation is a separate design research task; the immediate correctness fix does not require it.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- plugins/python3-development/agents/swarm-task-planner.md (template to fix)\\n- plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md (template to fix)\\n- plugins/python3-development/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_format.py (has_yaml_frontmatter, parse_yaml_frontmatter)\\n- plugins/python3-development/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py (parse_task_content, _create_empty_task_data)\\n- plugins/python3-development/scripts/split_task_file.py (parse_tasks_with_body)\\n- plugins/python3-development/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py (authorized writer)\\n- plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md (format spec, document script-only writes policy)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 the template fix is self-contained\\n- Blocks: #338 (SAM task planner should include relevant skills) \u2014 that item adds a skills: field to task frontmatter, which only has effect if frontmatter is parseable; the fenced-block bug prevents skills: from being read\\n- Related: #105 (SAM parser regex false positive on Task Summary) \u2014 both are parser correctness issues in implementation_manager.py\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\nEffort: Medium. Template fix is Small; adding format validation and documenting script-only writes lifts to Medium. Pure YAML multi-document evaluation is a separate research task if pursued.\\nBlockers: None \u2014 RT-ICA APPROVED. Root cause verified in both agent files.\\n\",\"digest\":\"30addd3681688bc70c336f5d770ce93357465ea0da36b477e6694e257fbe48ed\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCOSVg\"}"}